  "Q10": {
    "answer": "Between July 18, 2026 and November 14, 2026, at least seven Federal Register documents matter to an F-1 student planning post-graduation work in the U.S.: (1) FR Doc. 2026-20660 ('Optional Practical Training Fees,' Proposed Rule, published Oct. 8, 2026, 91 FR 64566): proposes requiring SEVP-certified schools to pay $70,000 for initial OPT and $30,000 for subsequent OPT (including STEM OPT if the $70,000 fee was previously paid) prior to DSO recommendation; NOT in force (NPRM; rule comments closed Nov. 9, 2026; PRA comments due Dec. 7, 2026). (2) FR Doc. 2026-19554 (Proclamation 11069, 'Restriction on Entry of Certain Nonimmigrant Workers,' Presidential Document, published Sept. 23, 2026, signed Sept. 18, 2026, 91 FR 60497): extends through Sept. 21, 2027 the entry restriction and $100,000 payment requirement for H-1B workers outside the U.S. or seeking admission via consular/POE notification to effectuate an H-1B petition; IN FORCE (effective Sept. 21, 2026). (3) FR Doc. 2026-17324 ('Fee for Certain H-1B Petitions,' Proposed Rule, published Aug. 25, 2026, 91 FR 54817, with correction C1-2026-17324 published Sept. 10, 2026, 91 FR 57516): proposes a $103,265 additional filing fee on all cap-subject H-1B petitions (including advanced-degree exemption petitions); NOT in force (NPRM). (4) FR Doc. 2026-20955 ('Removal of Automatic Extensions for Certain Employment Authorization Documents,' Final Rule, published Oct. 14, 2026, 91 FR 65306): finalizes the Oct. 30, 2025 interim final rule ending automatic EAD renewal extensions for certain EAD renewal categories (note 2026-14439 preamble 91 FR 45024, 45101 confirms the separate 180-day STEM OPT extension under 8 CFR 274a.12(b)(6)(iv) remains in place); IN FORCE (effective Oct. 14, 2026). (5) FR Doc. 2026-18631 ('Eliminating the Discretionary 60-Day Grace Period,' Proposed Rule, published Sept. 11, 2026, 91 FR 57807): proposes removing 8 CFR 214.1(l)(2) to eliminate the up-to-60-day grace period upon cessation of employment for H-1B, O-1, TN, L-1, and E workers; NOT in force (NPRM; comments closed Nov. 10, 2026). (6) FR Doc. 2026-16231 ('9-11 Response and Biometric Entry-Exit Fee for H-1B and L-1 Visas,' Final Rule, published Aug. 10, 2026, 91 FR 51360): requires covered employers (50+ U.S. employees with >50% in H-1B/L-1 status) to pay the 9-11 Biometric Fee on all H-1B/L-1 extension-of-status petitions; IN FORCE (effective Sept. 9, 2026). (7) FR Doc. 2026-16313 ('Mandatory Electronic Filing (e-Filing),' Interim Final Rule, published Aug. 11, 2026, 91 FR 51924): authorizes USCIS to mandate e-filing for certain immigration benefit requests and sets waiver procedures; IN FORCE (effective Aug. 11, 2026). (Other potentially relevant items include E.O. 14431, FR Doc. 2026-19555, Presidential Document, Sept. 23, 2026, 91 FR 60501, in force, directing H-1B integrity/interagency coordination; Proposed Rule 2026-20941, Oct. 14, 2026, 91 FR 65119, not in force, proposing to remove 8 CFR 214.1(c)(5) deference to prior approvals; and Correction 2026-14698, July 21, 2026, 91 FR 45637, in force, correcting the H.R. 1 fees/EAD validity IFR.)",
    "basis": "FR Doc. 2026-20660 (91 FR 64566); FR Doc. 2026-19554 (91 FR 60497); FR Doc. 2026-19555 (91 FR 60501); FR Doc. 2026-17324 (91 FR 54817) and C1-2026-17324 (91 FR 57516); FR Doc. 2026-20955 (91 FR 65306); FR Doc. 2026-18631 (91 FR 57807); FR Doc. 2026-16231 (91 FR 51360); FR Doc. 2026-16313 (91 FR 51924); FR Doc. 2026-20941 (91 FR 65119); FR Doc. 2026-14698 (91 FR 45637).",
    "uncertainty": "For 2026-20955, 2026-16231, 2026-16313, 2026-20941, 2026-17324, C1-2026-17324, and 2026-14698, summaries rely on Federal Register search metadata and abstracts rather than full-text reading due to context budget limits."
